      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "MY FRIEND BEC (2) put in a much better performance last start when in the placings at Gosford behind Morning Daylight (22.16) in a Free For All. Led around the bend before fighting on well and should give a sight. Recorded one of the quickest times on the card last start despite being beaten. Makes plenty of appeal. DANIEL KEEPING (1) had been racing in honest fashion recording two placings in a row before finishing fifth (18.83) at Dubbo latest. Safe beginner who draws ideally on the inside. Deserves plenty of respect. BUSY MAN (8) was game in defeat off the inside draw last start, finishing second and beaten 1.5 lengths (18.04) behind Summer Dream at Richmond. Ran one of the fastest times on the program last start despite finishing in the minors. Can measure up. RAY OF EVE (7) comes back from a let-up as a top three prospect.",
